 "equipment_type": "Energy recovery / DOAS make-up air unit controller (legacy)",
 "applies_to": "Valent VPR, VPRE, VPRC/P and VPRX series units with the JENEsys controller, software version 4 (legacy controller).",
 "summary": "Valent's older JENEsys controller (software version 4) supports optional, licensed BACnet IP and BACnet MS/TP. The BMS can enable BAS occupancy control and send the occupancy command, disable cooling or heating, issue an emergency shutdown, reset alarms, write space, supply, humidity, CO2 and static pressure setpoints, and send sensor values and fan and damper signals that override the unit's own. It reads temperatures, humidity, enthalpy, pressures, fan speeds, outputs, compressor and heat stages, alarms, occupancy mode and unit mode.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "Software version 4",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Writable points are the ones shaded as 'Editable' in the manual's BACnet Setpoint List; the manual says they accept writes at priorities 2-5 and 7-16.",
  "BAS-reported sensor values (marked * in the manual) override any hardwired sensors while written.",
  "BACnet is a licensed option; without the license the settings can be viewed but not changed.",
  "Instances AV 33, BV 31 and BV 44 are not listed.",
  "Engineering units are not printed in the BACnet table.",
  "Source: BACnet Setpoint List, manual pages 34-36 (108 objects)."
 ],
